2026-11-06T21:05:52.5906990Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5907720Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5908500Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5910280Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5911470Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5911900Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5912340Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5913290Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5913980Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5914410Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5916310Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5917630Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5918920Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5919820Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5920350Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5921140Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5922220Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5922800Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5923980Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5925900Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5926460Z 
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5926840Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5928090Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-06T21:05:52.5936190Z 
